      "body": "Follow-up to #1571 (part of #1569).\n\nWhen a stream piped by a `fromNodeHandler` handler fails, the handler rejects with h3's internal `kHandled` signal: the response is already committed and the error has been reported to the app `onError` hook. The `onError()` middleware treated that signal as an error:\n\n- its hook was called with a bogus `HTTPError` 500 (`cause: Symbol(h3.handled)`)\n- it re-threw that error, so the app `onError` hook ran a second time\n- the error was rendered and its JSON body appended to the already committed response (`item1{\"status\": 500, ...}` with status 200)\n\nThe middleware now re-throws `kHandled` untouched, without calling its hook.\n\nMiddleware-registered hooks still do not see stream errors (only the app `onError` config hook does). Reporting them there too would need a separate design.\n\nTest: a new `app.test.ts` case pipes a failing stream with an `onError()` middleware registered. It fails on `main` and passes with the change. Lint, typecheck and the full suite pass.\n\n🤖 Generated with AI assistant\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Errors from a Node response stream no longer trigger the middleware error callback after the response has started; the application error hook still receives the error.\n  * The response content already sent to the client remains unchanged.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
